\title{The Ford-Fulkerson algorithm}
\date{2026-11-12T17:58:18Z}
\tag{algorithms}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{We can now define the \em{Ford-Fulkerson algorithm}, which is similar to the [greedy flow algorithm](00S3) but uses the [residual network](00SB) instead of the original network to find augmenting paths.  Every time an augmenting path traverses a "forwards" edge in the residual network, we add flow to the corresponding edge in #{G}; when an augmenting path traverses a "backwards" edge, we \em{subtract} flow from the corresponding edge in #{G}.}

\transclude{00SE}   % Ford-Fulkerson

\p{We take a moment to record a few observations/lemmas about this algorithm.}

\transclude{00SF}   % Augmenting preserves flow validity
\transclude{00SG}   % Augmenting increases flow value
\transclude{00SH}   % F-F terminates
